--
N5008 [temp.inst]/3.1, /4: implicitly instantiating vec<block> instantiates
the declarations, not the definitions, of the members of its member class
`temporary'; a definition is instantiated when used.  The front end
deferred the member functions of a class template specialization but not
those of its member classes, so temporary::get and release were converted
for vec<block> with block still incomplete and dropped ("dropped the body
of function 'get'", bin53).  They are now deferred alike.  Found from
libstdc++'s vector<_Tp>::_Temporary_value for the incomplete
__pool_resource::_BigBlock (cpp11_libstdcxx_header_drops/
test_memory_resource.desc).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program,
and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
